"""Triton implementation of ``aten::_sparse_csr_prod``.

The operator reduces a 2-D sparse CSR tensor along ``dim`` and returns another
sparse CSR tensor. Exactly like the sum sibling, only stored entries
participate: an implicit (unstored) zero is *not* multiplied in, which is why
the result structure follows the layout and not the values. Storing an explicit
zero does drive the product to zero, as it would in a dense reduction.

* ``dim=[1]`` (row reduction) keeps one entry per row that stores at least one
  value, at column 0. Rows are contiguous CSR segments, so the kernel walks the
  segment and multiplies.
* ``dim=[0]`` (column reduction) keeps one entry per column that stores at
  least one value, in ascending column order. Products cannot be accumulated
  with atomics, so the payload is stably sorted by column first; every column's
  segment is then contiguous and one program per column multiplies it.
* ``dim=[0, 1]`` (or an empty ``dim``) folds everything into one entry, present
  only when the input stores anything at all.
"""

